From: Aspartame GTK4 migration
Subject: [PATCH] toolkit: call Gtk.Widget snapshot vfunc with explicit instance

PyGObject exposes the inherited GTK4 snapshot vfunc with a binding quirk:
``super().do_snapshot(snapshot)`` dispatches to ``Widget.snapshot`` without
the widget instance and raises ``TypeError`` during every toolbar button
render.  The explicit base-class call preserves the normal Gtk.Button
snapshot before drawing Sugar's arrow indicator.

---
 src/sugar4/graphics/toolbarbox.py | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/sugar4/graphics/toolbarbox.py b/src/sugar4/graphics/toolbarbox.py
--- a/src/sugar4/graphics/toolbarbox.py
+++ b/src/sugar4/graphics/toolbarbox.py
@@ -196,7 +196,7 @@ class ToolbarButton(ToolButton):
 
     def do_snapshot(self, snapshot):
         """GTK4 drawing implementation with arrow indicator."""
-        super().do_snapshot(snapshot)
+        Gtk.Widget.do_snapshot(self, snapshot)
 
         width = self.get_width()
         height = self.get_height()
